<title>USA: Video Display amends 9-mos results, Q4 dips.</title>
<headline>Video Display amends 9-mos results, Q4 dips.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 mos. ended	  12 mos. ended</p>
<p>		     2/28/97	2/29/96     2/28/97     2/29/96</p>
<p> Net sales    $15,537,000 $12,025,000 $53,865,000 $48,112,000</p>
<p> Net income	 442,000     466,000   1,898,000   1,779,000</p>
<p> Earnings per share  0.11	  0.12	  0.48	  0.45</p>
<p> Avg shrs	 3,960,000   3,968,000   3,960,000   3,968,000</p>
<p>			9 mos. as amended  9 mos. (previous report)</p>
<p>		    11/30/96     11/30/95    11/30/96    11/30/95</p>
<p> Net sales    $38,328,000 $36,087,000 $38,328,000 $36,087,000</p>
<p> Net income     1,456,000   1,313,000   1,896,000   1,313,000</p>
<p> Earnings per share  0.37	  0.33	  0.48	  0.33</p>
<p>NOTE: The company restated its results lower for the first three quarters of fiscal year 1997 to reflect reductions in gross profit margins, resulting in a reduction of the carrying value of product inventories.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
